learn=[('Annotate truthfully', 'readOnlyHint allows read-only calls to run concurrently. The app measures actual handler intervals and reports overlap. An annotation does not enforce behavior or guarantee a particular schedule.'), ('Return useful tool errors', 'A controlled local endpoint really returns HTTP 503. The handler returns isError: true with context. A second experiment throws a controlled exception so you can inspect the SDK-converted error result.'), ('Keep tool and query outcomes separate', 'The SDK can deliver a tool error to Claude and still finish the query successfully. This is distinct from a model API, process or transport failure, which can still terminate a run.'), ('Send images as actual bytes', 'The handler fetches a PNG from this app and returns raw base64 plus image/png. The chart is clearly labelled classroom sample data, not live weather. Inspect its image hash and the native image block.'), ('Embed resource content', 'The report uses a classroom URI with inline Markdown text. The URI identifies the supplied content; the app does not read a file from that URI. Text, images and resources can appear together.'), ('Return exact structured fields', 'The structured experiment returns a sample chart and its exact JSON points. Compare the native forwarded blocks: structured data, image and resource remain, while a duplicate text sentinel is omitted.')]
document('/','Custom tools. <em>Richer results.</em>','Annotations, tool errors, images, inline resources and exact JSON.','<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Annotate</b><p>Truthful hints and measured timing</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Handle</b><p>Useful errors; distinct query outcome</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Return</b><p>Images, resources and exact JSON</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Explore advanced custom tools</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Advanced-tool experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="parallel-readonly">Read-only weather calls · measure overlap</option><option value="friendly-error">Friendly error · actual local HTTP 503</option><option value="uncaught-error">Uncaught exception · SDK error conversion</option><option value="image">Image block · classroom sample chart</option><option value="resource">Resource block · inline Markdown report</option><option value="structured">Structured JSON + image + resource</option><option value="mixed">Mixed text + image + resource</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run advanced-tool experiment →</button><p class="meta">Real SDK calls. Live weather is external; HTTP 503 is an intentional local failure. Rich results use clearly labelled classroom sample data. No separate custom MCP server is needed.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>SDK reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>The server is registered as advanced. The handlers carry truthful annotations, and the small schemas use alwaysLoad for this lesson.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Actual available tools</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="handler-panel"><h2>Actual handler timing and returned content</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="handlers" class="language-json">[]</code></pre><p>Intervals use one monotonic clock. The weather handlers include an explicitly labelled 700 ms teaching delay to make overlapping intervals easier to observe. A hint alone is not evidence of overlap.</p></section><section class="step" id="native-panel"><h2>Native SDK tool-result projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="native" class="language-json">[]</code></pre><p>This projects actual user tool_result blocks: error flags, text and image metadata. Base64 bytes are counted rather than dumped into this panel. Compare these forwarded blocks with the handler’s original result.</p></section><section class="step" id="artifact-panel" hidden><h2>The PNG returned by the chart tool</h2><img src="/demo-chart.png" alt="Classroom sample chart with values 58, 59, 61, 63 and 62; not live weather" style="width:100%;max-width:1000px"><p>The handler fetches this exact bundled image over local HTTP; the evidence includes its byte count and SHA-256 hash. No image is invented to replace a failed tool call.</p></section><section class="step" id="resource-panel"><h2>Inline report preview</h2><div id="report" class="markdown-body"></div><p>In Resource mode this preview renders the actual inline text. Its classroom URI is an identifier, not an instruction to read a file.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Verify errors, overlap and forwarded blocks</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>For structured data, compare structuredMarkerForwarded with duplicateTextForwarded. Images and inline report content should remain. For tool errors, compare toolErrorResults with the final query status.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Handlers</th><th>Overlap</th><th>Tool errors</th><th>Forwarded types</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ol id="events"></ol></section>','<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Make tool behavior observable and return the right result shape.',cards(learn))
env='ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3123\n# Optional on Windows: CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe'
runsteps=[('Prepare the runtime', 'Use Node.js 24 or later. Windows may need Git Bash. This application needs a funded model API account, and the weather experiment needs access to Open-Meteo.', 'node --version\nnpm --version'), ('Install and create your .env file', 'From presentations run these commands. Preserve an existing .env, enter your API key privately and keep credentials on the server.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson23-advanced-tools\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the web application', 'Keep the server running. The friendly-error and chart CLI exercises call this app over local HTTP, so they also require it. No separate MCP service is started.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3123'), ('Measure read-only calls and inspect errors', 'Compare actual handler intervals. Then run the intentional HTTP 503 and uncaught exception. Tool error flags and the final query status are different evidence.', 'npm run sample:env -- parallel-readonly\nnpm run sample:env -- friendly-error\nnpm run sample:env -- uncaught-error'), ('Inspect image and resource content', 'The image is bundled classroom sample data served over actual local HTTP. The report carries its content inline. Inspect native tool-result blocks as well as the formatted answer.', 'npm run sample:env -- image\nnpm run sample:env -- resource'), ('Compare structured and mixed results', 'Structured mode pairs exact JSON with image and resource blocks, and tests a duplicate-text sentinel. Mixed mode keeps ordinary text alongside image and resource content.', 'npm run sample:env -- structured\nnpm run sample:env -- mixed\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Keep the actual key private. No Managed Agents agent ID or environment ID is required. No duplicate snapshot is included.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use the URL printed by startup. If another app occupies the port, change PORT and restart. If API credit is unavailable, add credit to the account used by this key. Weather HTTP or validation failures remain visible; no cached result replaces a failed live call. The error and chart CLI exercises require this web server to be running on the same PORT.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install, configure and inspect advanced tool results.',body)
specs=[('Validate the experiment', 'src/agent.ts', 'return { mode:', 'Accept only the seven classroom tasks. Browser input does not supply executable handlers or arbitrary service URLs.', 0, 1), ('Annotate tool behavior', 'src/tools.ts', 'export const READ_ONLY =', 'These hints describe read-only behavior. They do not enforce it. The app measures overlap instead of assuming a schedule from the annotation.', 1, 3), ('Register the advanced server', 'src/tools.ts', 'return createSdkMcpServer({', 'Wrap the selected tool definitions in an in-process MCP server. The server runs in this Node host while the model remains remote.', 1, 2), ('Configure tool access', 'src/agent.ts', 'tools: [],', 'Remove built-ins and register only the selected custom tools. The full advanced namespace is pre-approved for this classroom experiment.', 1, 2), ('Start the actual query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query(', 'Streaming input keeps the in-process MCP exchange open. The SDK manages the model and tool loop; the host reads actual messages.', 1, 2), ('Measure handler intervals', 'src/tools.ts', 'const startMs = now();', 'Record start and end times on a monotonic clock. Weather includes a labelled seven-hundred-millisecond teaching delay. Only intersecting observed intervals count as overlap.', 2, 3), ('Return a friendly tool failure', 'src/tools.ts', 'const result = friendlyFailure(response.status);', 'An intentional local HTTP 503 becomes a composed isError result. It is not a successful data response, and the model is asked not to retry.', 3, 2), ('Observe exception conversion', 'src/tools.ts', 'throw new Error("Classroom upstream unavailable (intentional)");', 'This controlled uncaught handler exception is converted by the SDK MCP server to an error tool result. Other kinds of SDK or transport failures can still end a query.', 3, 2), ('Encode an actual PNG', 'src/tools.ts', 'const image = {', 'The handler fetches the bundled sample PNG and returns raw base64 with image/png. The source image is labelled classroom data, not live weather.', 3, 2), ('Embed a report by URI', 'src/tools.ts', 'export function resourceBlock()', 'The resource carries its Markdown text inline. The classroom URI is a label; no filesystem read from that URI is implied.', 3, 2), ('Return exact structured fields', 'src/tools.ts', 'return { content, structuredContent: SAMPLE };', 'Structured JSON is forwarded with the image and inline resource. The redundant text sentinel is not forwarded in the observed SDK tool result.', 3, 2), ('Inspect native tool-result blocks', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (message.type === "user"', 'Project actual native tool results, preserving error flags and block metadata. Do not dump base64 into the interface or infer forwarding from the model answer alone.', 2, 1), ('Render text beside evidence', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer")', 'Sanitize and format model Markdown. Keep model text separate from handler timings, original block types and actual SDK-forwarded results.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','MCP handler','HTTP + assets']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={1:3,2:6,3:6,4:4,5:3,6:4,7:4,8:1,9:5,10:8,11:1,12:6,13:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
