reference=[('Annotations are not guards', 'readOnlyHint permits concurrency but does not guarantee it. The other three hints are descriptive. This app records intervals and labels a 700 ms teaching delay; the reported overlap is an observation, not a benchmark.'), ('Controlled error demonstrations', 'The HTTP 503 endpoint and thrown exception are intentional classroom failures. Both travel through real SDK tool calls. A success query status does not convert the error into successful data. API authentication, budget, process and transport failures can still terminate a run.'), ('Original and forwarded results', 'Handler evidence shows what the function returned. Native-result projections show the SDK user tool_result content after conversion. Image bytes are represented by MIME type and length. The structured-data experiment checks the duplicate-text sentinel directly.'), ('Sample chart and inline resource', 'The bundled PNG uses fixed points 58, 59, 61, 63, 62. It is not weather fetched from Open-Meteo. The report embeds text using a classroom URI. Neither URI access nor file creation is implied.'), ('Tool search and process boundaries', 'This small server uses alwaysLoad for its schemas. Deferred tool search is not demonstrated. In-process describes the custom server, not the Claude Code child runtime or remote model service.'), ('Other result types', 'Audio, resource links and binary resources are reference topics here. Only text, PNG images, inline text resources and structured JSON are executed. Python differs for structuredContent and binary resources; this application teaches TypeScript.'), ('Rebuild the sample chart', 'The PNG is bundled, so Python is not needed to run the app. To regenerate it, install matplotlib in your Python environment and run python scripts/create-chart.py. Keep the classroom-data label.')]

document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Thirteen source-linked steps explain metadata, failures and rich result blocks.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 23 · Advanced custom tools\n\nBased on Lesson23_Custom_Tools_Advanced.pptx. Five linked student pages with large text and coloured code in every UML step.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson23-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson23-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson23-advanced-tools` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3123 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit, model access and internet are required. Windows may require Git Bash. No separate MCP server is needed.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nCopy .env.example only if .env does not exist. Enter your key privately and restart after edits. The startup script loads this file; existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo Managed Agents IDs are required. Real .env, media, private workspaces and dependencies are excluded from Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Custom tools: official SDK documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/custom-tools)\n- [Open-Meteo weather API](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs)\n- [Open-Meteo licence and attribution](https://open-meteo.com/en/licence)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. `npm test` checks interval overlap, error flags, native image projections, resource content and startup without paid model calls.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 23 student pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
